1022694.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['No business being in NATO': Presidential hopeful Melenchon pitches radical new course for France]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135652487.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/no-business-being-in-nato-presidential-hopeful-melenchon-pitches-radical-new-course-for-france/articleshow/135652487.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/no-business-being-in-nato-presidential-hopeful-melenchon-pitches-radical-new-course-for-france/articleshow/135652487.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T12:27:09+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vijaya Srivastava</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135653483,imgsize-86944.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[How a 5-year-old turned garden cucumbers into a pickle business]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135570299.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-donovan-atkinson-the-5-year-old-who-turned-cucumbers-from-his-familys-garden-into-a-pickle-business-and-sold-more-than-500-jars-from-his-roadside-stand/articleshow/135570299.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/meet-donovan-atkinson-the-5-year-old-who-turned-cucumbers-from-his-familys-garden-into-a-pickle-business-and-sold-more-than-500-jars-from-his-roadside-stand/articleshow/135570299.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T13:51:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135570393,imgsize-1706409.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ancient Maya cities used red pigment in temples; study finds it left mercury in lakes for centuries]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135640059.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Ancient Maya civilization used a red pigment made of mercury-rich cinnabar for decoration and rituals. This practice led to significant mercury contamination of nearby lakes and ecosystems. Research indicates that rising mercury levels impacted aquatic organisms and may have affected human health. Previous studies have also shown similar contamination at various Maya sites, raising concerns about widespread environmental impact.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/ancient-mayas-vivid-red-pigment-a-toxic-legacy-of-mercury-contamination-revealed-in-new-study/articleshow/135640059.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/archaeology/ancient-mayas-vivid-red-pigment-a-toxic-legacy-of-mercury-contamination-revealed-in-new-study/articleshow/135640059.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T13:48:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135640309,imgsize-1111189.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Florida man loses down-payment credit after depositing home-sale proceeds in joint account]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135602427.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Florida divorce case involved a man seeking credit for his premarital contributions towards a jointly owned house. He sold his house and deposited the proceeds into a joint account with his wife. The court ruled that money became marital property when used to benefit jointly owned property. While the husband's credits for the down payment were reversed, his expenses after separation were upheld.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-man-sold-his-georgia-home-put-the-proceeds-in-a-joint-account-and-used-the-money-to-build-a-house-with-his-wife-after-she-filed-for-divorce-an-appeals-court-ruled-the-down-payment-was-marital-property/articleshow/135602427.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-florida-man-sold-his-georgia-home-put-the-proceeds-in-a-joint-account-and-used-the-money-to-build-a-house-with-his-wife-after-she-filed-for-divorce-an-appeals-court-ruled-the-down-payment-was-marital-property/articleshow/135602427.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T12:57:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135602537,imgsize-1811125.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[She began with a fundraiser to feed just 25 schoolchildren; today, Kenyan entrepreneur Wawira Njiru employs 6,000 people, and her organisation serves 730,000 children every day]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135604729.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Wawira Njiru's inspiring journey started with a simple goal: to provide meals for just 25 schoolchildren in Kenya. This small effort blossomed into Food4Education, which now delivers over 700,000 meals each day. Through innovative solutions like Tap2Eat, parents can easily contribute to their children's meals. Njiru's ambition is to extend this impactful model beyond Kenya, tackling childhood hunger throughout Africa and enhancing both food security and educational opportunities.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/she-began-with-a-fundraiser-to-feed-just-25-schoolchildren-today-kenyan-entrepreneur-wawira-njiru-employs-6000-people-and-her-organisation-serves-730000-children-every-day/articleshow/135604729.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/she-began-with-a-fundraiser-to-feed-just-25-schoolchildren-today-kenyan-entrepreneur-wawira-njiru-employs-6000-people-and-her-organisation-serves-730000-children-every-day/articleshow/135604729.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T12:53:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Lifestyle Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135605109,imgsize-1969823.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[DNA analysis reveals 87 rice pests in bird and bat diets in West Africa]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135570309.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/bird-and-bat-droppings-reveal-87-rice-pest-species-in-their-diets-with-dna-analysis-uncovering-2276-feeding-interactions-across-34-predator-species-in-west-african-rice-fields/articleshow/135570309.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/wildlife/bird-and-bat-droppings-reveal-87-rice-pest-species-in-their-diets-with-dna-analysis-uncovering-2276-feeding-interactions-across-34-predator-species-in-west-african-rice-fields/articleshow/135570309.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-11-08T13:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135570464,imgsize-2111022.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Canadian contractor's $778 cabin visit fee rejected by tribunal]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135610348.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]><